# Lab 4: Active Footprinting Report (`vulnbank.org`)

## Scope & Ethical Boundaries
This activity focused strictly on safe, non-intrusive active footprinting against `https://vulnbank.org/`, an intentionally vulnerable training web application[cite: 1, 2]. No exploitation, vulnerability attacks, brute-forcing, credential abuse, or destructive testing were performed[cite: 2].

---

## 1. Own Host Setup (Reconnaissance Machine)
Active reconnaissance was performed from a Kali Linux virtual machine running in Oracle VirtualBox[cite: 1, 2].

| Component | Configuration |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Operating System** | Kali Linux (`kali-linux-2026.3-virtualbox-amd64`)[cite: 1] |
| **Hostname / User** | `koi` (`kali@koi`)[cite: 1, 2] |
| **Hypervisor** | Oracle VirtualBox[cite: 1] |
| **Network Mode** | Bridged Adapter (`Realtek PCIe GbE Family Controller`)[cite: 1] |
| **Interface & IPv4** | `eth0` (`UP`), `192.168.100.131/24` (subnet `192.168.100.0/24`)[cite: 1] |
| **Default Gateway** | `192.168.100.254` via `eth0`[cite: 1] |
| **Tools Used** | `ip`, `host`, `nslookup`, `ping`, `nmap`, `curl`, Firefox[cite: 2, 3, 4, 6, 7] |

### Evidence
![VirtualBox Bridged Network and Kali IP/Route Output](screenshots/part1-vbox-network-and-ip.png)[cite: 1]

---

## 2. Target Setup & Initial Discovery
The reconnaissance target was the hosted training web application at `https://vulnbank.org/`[cite: 1, 2].

| Component | Configuration / Observation |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Target URL / Host** | `https://vulnbank.org/` (`vulnbank.org`) |
| **Resolved IPv4** | `172.67.134.11`, `104.21.5.243`[cite: 2] |
| **Resolved IPv6** | `2606:4700:3035::ac43:860b`, `2606:4700:3034::6815:5f3`[cite: 2] |
| **DNS Service Binding** | `HTTPS` record advertising `alpn="h3,h2"`[cite: 2] |
| **ICMP Reachability** | `ping -c 3 vulnbank.org` -> 3 received, 0% packet loss (~20.1–25.8 ms RTT)[cite: 2] |
| **Web Ports Scanned** | `80/tcp` (`open`, `http`, `Cloudflare http proxy`), `443/tcp` (`open`, `ssl/http`, `Cloudflare http proxy`)[cite: 3] |

### Evidence
![DNS Lookup and ICMP Ping Results for vulnbank.org](screenshots/part2-dns-ping.png)[cite: 2]

![Nmap Service Scan on Ports 80 and 443](screenshots/part2-nmap-80-443.png)[cite: 3]

