---

## 3. Findings & Evidence

### 3.1 HTTP Response Headers (`curl -I`)
A read-only header request to `https://vulnbank.org/` returned `HTTP/2 200` on `Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:01:30 GMT` with `content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8`, `server: cloudflare`, `cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC`, `cf-ray: a5cfbf486c042af5-SIN` (Singapore edge), `alt-svc: h3=":443"; ma=86400`, and `access-control-allow-origin: *`[cite: 6].

![HTTP Response Headers for vulnbank.org](screenshots/part3-curl-headers.png)[cite: 6]

### 3.2 TLS Handshake & Certificate Inspection (`curl -vI`)
A verbose HTTPS connection check confirmed a `TLSv1.3` handshake (`TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384` with `X25519MLKEM768`) negotiating HTTP/2 (`h2`) for certificate subject `CN=vulnbank.org` (valid from `Oct 20 23:36:02 2026 GMT`), while an initial IPv6 attempt reported `Network is unreachable` before connecting over IPv4 (`104.21.5.243:443`)[cite: 7].

![Verbose TLS and HTTP/2 Handshake Output](screenshots/part3-curl-tls.png)[cite: 7]

### 3.3 Public Metadata (`robots.txt`)
Fetching `https://vulnbank.org/robots.txt` returned policy comments describing content signals (`search`, `ai-input`, `ai-train`) and copyright signal notices[cite: 8].

![vulnbank.org robots.txt Output](screenshots/part3-robots-txt.png)[cite: 8]

---

## 4. Analysis, Limitations & Recommendations

### 4.1 What the Evidence Proves, Suggests, and Cannot Establish
* **Proves:** At capture time, `vulnbank.org` resolved via DNS to the recorded IPv4/IPv6 addresses and `HTTPS` ALPN hints, responded to `ping -c 3` with 0% packet loss, exposed `80/tcp` and `443/tcp` as `open` with `Cloudflare http proxy` banners, returned `HTTP/2 200` on `19 Nov 2026 14:01:30 GMT`, completed a `TLSv1.3` (`h2`) handshake for `CN=vulnbank.org`, and served a readable `robots.txt` file[cite: 2, 3, 6, 7, 8].
* **Suggests:** Traffic passes through Cloudflare reverse-proxy/CDN edge infrastructure (including Singapore routing `-SIN` and HTTP/3 advertisement), responses are generated dynamically (`cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC`), IPv6 routing from the VM was unavailable/unreachable in that test, and `access-control-allow-origin: *` indicates a wildcard cross-origin header on the observed response[cite: 2, 6, 7].
* **Cannot Establish:** The true origin server IP address, internal network architecture, underlying OS/application versions behind Cloudflare, or any confirmed exploitable vulnerability[cite: 2, 3, 6, 7, 8].

### 4.2 Limitations
* **Reverse Proxy / CDN Masking:** Cloudflare edge IPs and proxy banners conceal origin server identity and prevent direct origin banner or OS fingerprinting[cite: 2, 3, 6].
* **Point-in-Time Snapshot:** DNS responses, edge nodes, latency, and live HTTP responses reflect conditions at the moment of testing and may vary across times or networks[cite: 2, 6, 7].
* **Non-Intrusive Scope:** Limiting activity to safe footprinting on ports `80` and `443`—without brute-forcing, fuzzing, or exploitation—leaves unexamined paths and application internals untested[cite: 2, 3].

### 4.3 Defensive Recommendations

| Area / Observation | Recommended Defense |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Origin Exposure** | Restrict direct origin connections so traffic only enters through approved proxy/CDN IP ranges[cite: 3, 6]. |
| **Cross-Origin & HTTP Headers** | Scope `access-control-allow-origin` and other response headers to intended origins and security requirements rather than broad wildcards[cite: 6]. |
| **Transport & Protocol Hygiene** | Maintain current TLS/HTTP configurations and ensure IPv6/IPv4 dual-stack routing is intentionally configured and monitored[cite: 2, 7]. |
| **Patch & Verification Discipline** | Keep underlying application and server software updated and validate security posture through authorized testing rather than relying on banners alone[cite: 3]. |

### 4.4 Conclusion
This lab demonstrated how to conduct structured, safe active footprinting of `vulnbank.org` from Kali Linux (`koi`) while documenting verifiable evidence and distinguishing hard proof from inference[cite: 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8]. Recognizing reverse-proxy masking and non-intrusive testing boundaries helps keep reconnaissance accurate, ethical, and grounded in observable facts[cite: 2, 3, 6].
